
<%# removed all webflow data attributes %>

<div class="create-segment-form-wrapper">
  <div class="content-sub-wrapper modal w-clearfix">
    <h4 class="modal-header welcome-dash-content-container-header">Create Segment</h4>
    <%# added data and update-close-modals %>
    <a class="close-modal update-close-modals" href="#" data-parent="new-segment-div"></a>
  </div>
  <p class="modal-content-description">A segment is a group (subset) of your customers defined by filters that you set. Customers that match these filters are automatically added to the group over time.</p>
  <div class="segment-modal underline-div"></div>
  <div class="create-segment w-form">
    <form id="email-form-8" name="email-form-8">
      <label class="form-label list-name" for="Segment-Name-2">Segment name</label>
      <input class="segment-name text-field w-input" id="Segment-Name-2" maxlength="256" name="Segment-Name-2" placeholder="Ex. Customer created 3 days ago" type="text"><a class="button create-segment-button w-button" href="#">Create Segment</a>
    </form>
  </div>
  <p class="modal-paragraph segment tips"> &nbsp;TIP: You can setup automated drip campaigns to nurture customers or leads. First create segments for each key group of customers or leads, E.g:leads that became customers 3-6 days ago,followed by leads that became customers 7-14 days ago, etc. Then go to your campaigns page to set up automatic messages.</p><a class="button manage-segments w-button" href="#">Manage segments</a>
</div>
